senses.gloss:
--a son of पृषत and father of द्रौपदी, धृष्टद्युम्न and others; king of the पाञ्चालस्;
1: भा. IX. २२. 2; X. ५२. ११ [8]. वा. ९९. २१०; Vi. IV. १९. ७३.
stationed by जरासन्ध at the northern gate of मथुरा;
2: भा. X. ५०. ११ [7].
stationed at the southern gate during the siege of Gomanta;
3: Ib. X. ५२. ११ [8].
had been bound by the young पाण्डवस्;
4: Ib. X. [५६ (V) 2].
in the स्वयम्वर he held, Arjuna hit the mark in the form of a fish and won Drau- पदी;
5: Ib. I. १५. 7.
joined the पाण्डवस् in the कुरुक्षेत्र battle;
6: Ib. X. ७८ [(९५ V) १०].
went to स्यमन्तपञ्चक for solar eclipse.
7: Ib. X. ८२. २५.
[page२-143+ ४२]

--the king of the किम्पुरुषस् and Kinnaras (s.v.) stationed on the west during the siege of Gomanta;
1: भा. X. ५२. ११ [११]. वा. ४१. ३०.
stationed by जरासन्ध at the western gate of मथुरा;
2: Ib. X. ५० 11 [5].
attended the conference at कुण्डीन summoned by शाल्व.
3: Ib. X. ७६. 2 [9-१०].

--a son of ययाति and सर्मिष्ठा and father of Babhru and Satu;
1: भा. IX. १८, ३३ and ४१; २३. १४; Br. I. 1. १३३; वा. 1. १५६; ९३. १७; ९९. 7; Vi. IV. १७. 1.
after being refused by Yadu and Turvasu approached by ययाति; he also declined to part with his youth to his father and was therefore cursed to have no pleasures in life and to be wandering about the countries and oceans with no settled kingdom;
2: M. २४. ५४; ३२. १०; २३. १६-20; वा. ४५. ५०; Vi. IV. १०. 6, १३.
became over-lord of the south-eastern (west ब्र्। प्।, वा। प्। and वि। प्।) part of the kingdom;
3: M. ३४. ३०; वा. ४५. ९०; Vi. १०. ३१.
from him begins the Bhoja line.
4: M. ४८. 6.
